Page 1 of 4

Ted-E-Bear stacks his softest pillows between two chairs. He wants a reading fort big
enough for one bear and one enormous adventure.
Page 2 of 4

He pulls a blue blanket over the top—but whoomph! It slides down and buries him in a
woolly heap.
Page 3 of 4

Panda-Cake holds one corner while Ted clips the other. Inside their sturdy fort, Ted
switches on a lamp and opens a story they can share.
Page 4 of 4

Rain whispers at the window, but the little fort is cosy and bright. Ted decides the best
forts are not the biggest—they are the ones with room for a friend.
Questions for Ted-E-Bear’s Blanket Fort

Read the story together first. Use one question at each page, then the question at the end. Answers are below
the dotted line: fold them under or cover them while reading.
Page 1

Talk together: What does Ted want to make with the pillows?
Page 2
Talk together: What went wrong with the blanket?
Page 3
Talk together: How did Panda-Cake help the story begin?
Page 4
Talk together: What did Ted learn about a cosy fort?
After reading
Why did the fort stay up when Panda-Cake helped?
Answers (fold under before reading)

After reading: They held and clipped the blanket together. Panda-Cake held one corner while Ted clipped the
other.

