Page 1 of 4

Meow-inara curls beside the moonlit window, but every tiny sound makes her ears spring
up. Tomorrow’s concert keeps marching through her thoughts.
Page 2 of 4

Wise Owl chooses a bedtime story about a musician whose first note wobbled. She reads
slowly and leaves room between each sentence.
Page 3 of 4

Meow-inara breathes in during one quiet line and breathes out during the next. The
concert is still tomorrow, but it no longer fills the whole room.
Page 4 of 4

At last she feels sleepy. “My first note can wobble too,” she murmurs, closing her eyes
beneath the patient moon.
Questions for Meow-inara’s Moonlight Story

Read the story together first. Use one question at each page, then the question at the end. Answers are below
the dotted line: fold them under or cover them while reading.
Page 1

Talk together: Why can Meow-inara not settle?
Page 2
Talk together: Why might Wise Owl choose this particular story?
Page 3
Talk together: What helps Meow-inara’s thoughts become quieter?
Page 4
Talk together: What has Meow-inara accepted by the end?
After reading
How did the bedtime story help Meow-inara?
Answers (fold under before reading)

After reading: She accepted that her first note might wobble too. She listened, breathed slowly and stopped
expecting a perfect first note.

